# Check every text file out with LF endings, on every platform.
#
# This repository's tests read the repository back — the workflows, the
# changelog, .goreleaser.yaml, the README — and match them line by line and
# with `(?m)^…$` anchors. A checkout that rewrote those lines to CRLF fails
# four of them without a byte of the repository having changed: `on:` is no
# longer `on:`, and `var injected string` no longer ends where `$` looks for
# it. That is what Git's default core.autocrlf=true produces on Windows, so
# without this the Windows leg of the Build and test matrix — and any
# contributor cloning there — would depend on a git setting nobody in the
# project controls (#66).
* text=auto eol=lf
